message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it like this."
title: "A Bonding Experience: The Open-Source New Frontier of Z-Delamination Resistance (a hobbyist's field guide to Z-strength in FDM printing without tripping over patents, including a defensive publication of PinLoK, pinned infill)"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Matthew
    alias: The-Dorkknight
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-13"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Dorkknight/a-bonding-experience"
url: "https://the-dorkknight.github.io/a-bonding-experience/"
keywords:
  - 3D printing
  - fused filament fabrication
  - FDM
  - layer adhesion
  - interlayer strength
  - z-pinning
  - pinned infill
  - defensive publication
  - prior art
abstract: >-
  A lab notebook of twelve ways to make FDM prints stronger between layers without beads of
  different heights, judged with a 2-D bead-by-bead strength model and checked against published
  tests. Pinned Grid infill (PinLoK), building on Oak Ridge National Laboratory's Z-pinning, was
  the only method to clear a 7 % target by a wide margin in simulation (+16 to +27 % against
  solid infill of the same weight; theoretical, not tested). Section 9 is a defensive disclosure of PinLoK and its variations.
